Virtual Piano
=== start
¶A one-octave piano that you can play!
For the best experience, turn the music visualization off.¶

¶This bind stores a Key stream that detects which key you've pressed.¶
pressed: Key()

¶This stores a mapping from the keys you press to the notes they will play,
in both text form (to display the note being played) and a numeric text
literal (to convert into a number (#) and input into a Track list).¶
notemap: {
		'w': ["C" "1"]
		'3': ["C# / Db" "2"]
		'e': ["D" "3"]
		'4': ["D# / Eb" "4"]
		'r': ["E" "5"]
		't': ["F" "6"]
		'6': ["F# / Gb" "7"]
		'y': ["G" "8"]
		'7': ["G# / Ab" "9"]
		'u': ["A" "10"]
		'8': ["A# / Bb" "11"]
		'i': ["B" "12"]
		'o': ["C5" "13"]
	}

¶This function returns the note's name, based on which key was pressed.
If the key was not a valid note, it returns empty text.¶
ƒ returnText(key•"")•"" (notemap{key} ≠ ø) ? notemap{key}[1] ""

¶This function returns the note number corresponding to the key pressed in a list,
to be used as an input in a Track. If the key pressed is invalid, it returns an
empty list.¶
ƒ returnNote(key•"")•[] [
		(notemap{key} ≠ ø) ? (notemap{key}[2] → #) []
	]

¶This function takes in a numeric list and returns a Track with that note list.
Loop is off so that the note plays once when the key is pressed.¶
ƒ returnTrack(note•[#]) Track(note loop: false)

¶These two binds map define the color to make the corresponding key when
it is pressed and when it is not.¶
pressColor: Color(10 270 50°)
nullColor: Color(0 0 0°)

¶This plays the pressed key's corresponding track. Scale is chromatic so
that the tracks can access all semitones. Replay is set for when a valid
key is pressed, so that the track plays whenever the key is pressed, even
twice in a row.¶
Music(
	returnTrack(returnNote(pressed))
	scale: Music.chromatic
	replay: notemap{pressed} ≠ ø
)

¶Displaying the piano, the keys to press, and the note played when a key
is pressed.¶
Group(
	Stack('>' 1m)
	[
		Group(
			Row('>' -.3m)
			[
				Phrase(
					'▯'
					name: 'w'
					size: 3m
					color: pressed = 'w' ? pressColor nullColor
				)
				Phrase(
					'▮'
					name: '3'
					size: 3m
					color: pressed = '3' ? pressColor nullColor
				)
				Phrase(
					'▯'
					name: 'e'
					size: 3m
					color: pressed = 'e' ? pressColor nullColor
				)
				Phrase(
					'▮'
					name: '4'
					size: 3m
					color: pressed = '4' ? pressColor nullColor
				)
				Phrase(
					'▯'
					name: 'r'
					size: 3m
					color: pressed = 'r' ? pressColor nullColor
				)
				Phrase(
					'▯'
					name: 't'
					size: 3m
					color: pressed = 't' ? pressColor nullColor
				)
				Phrase(
					'▮'
					name: '6'
					size: 3m
					color: pressed = '6' ? pressColor nullColor
				)
				Phrase(
					'▯'
					name: 'y'
					size: 3m
					color: pressed = 'y' ? pressColor nullColor
				)
				Phrase(
					'▮'
					name: '7'
					size: 3m
					color: pressed = '7' ? pressColor nullColor
				)
				Phrase(
					'▯'
					name: 'u'
					size: 3m
					color: pressed = 'u' ? pressColor nullColor
				)
				Phrase(
					'▮'
					name: '8'
					size: 3m
					color: pressed = '8' ? pressColor nullColor
				)
				Phrase(
					'▯'
					name: 'i'
					size: 3m
					color: pressed = 'i' ? pressColor nullColor
				)
				Phrase(
					'▯'
					name: 'o'
					size: 3m
					color: pressed = 'o' ? pressColor nullColor
				)
			]
		)

		Group(
			Row('>' 1.1m)
			[
				Phrase('w')
				Phrase('3')
				Phrase('e')
				Phrase('4')
				Phrase('r t')
				Phrase('6')
				Phrase('y')
				Phrase('7')
				Phrase('u')
				Phrase('8')
				Phrase('i  o')
			]
		)
		Phrase(returnText(pressed))
	]
)
